{"ref":"relic:chaos-rosalia","lead":[{"k":"p","c":["Chaos Rosalia is a relic located in ",{"t":"Astral Stair","r":"stage:astral-stair"},". Once collected, it permanently allows ",{"i":"Sprite-Yatta_Cavallo.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"character:yatta-cavallo"}," ",{"t":"Yatta Cavallo","r":"character:yatta-cavallo"}," to morph ",{"i":"Sprite-Cherry_Bomb.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"weapon:cherry-bomb"}," ",{"t":"Cherry Bomb","r":"weapon:cherry-bomb"}," into ",{"i":"Sprite-Yatta_Daikarin.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"weapon:yatta-daikarin"}," ",{"t":"Yatta Daikarin","r":"weapon:yatta-daikarin"}," upon reaching level 80."]}],"infobox":[{"title":"Relic","rows":[{"label":"Release","cells":[["12 June 2023 (Update)"]]},{"label":"ID","cells":[["RELIC_ROSALIA"]]},{"label":"Effects","cells":[["Morphs ",{"t":"Yatta Cavallo","r":"character:yatta-cavallo"}," at level 80 into a stronger form that evolves their ",{"t":"main weapon","r":"weapon:yatta-daikarin"},"."]]},{"label":"Location","cells":[["Located in ",{"t":"Astral Stair","r":"stage:astral-stair"},"."]]}]}],"sections":[{"id":"obtaining","title":"Obtaining","blocks":[{"k":"p","c":["Chaos Rosalia is located to the northeast of the starting area in ",{"t":"Astral Stair","r":"stage:astral-stair"}," in the top row of rooms, where it can be found in the last room. Its location is tracked by a green arrow on the player's screen. Once collected, it will no longer appear on the map."]},{"k":"p","c":["Alternatively, Chaos Rosalia can be unlocked in the ",{"i":"Sprite-Forbidden_Scrolls_of_Morbane.png","w":16,"h":16,"r":"relic:forbidden-scrolls-of-morbane"}," ",{"t":"Forbidden Scrolls of Morbane","r":"relic:forbidden-scrolls-of-morbane"}," by casting the spell \"coldwaterhotwater\"."]}],"subs":[]},{"id":"gallery","title":"Gallery","blocks":[{"k":"gallery","items":[{"i":"Sprite-Chaos_Rosalia_(old).png","w":120,"h":120,"c":["The old design of Chaos Rosalia icon."]}]}],"subs":[]},{"id":"update-history","title":"Update history","blocks":[{"k":"p","c":["This information has been manually compiled. Some updates may not be included yet."]},{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["hidden 17 August 2023 (Update):"],"sub":{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["Updated icon."]}]}}]},{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["update 12 June 2023 (Update):"],"sub":{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["Added to game."]}]}}]}],"subs":[]},{"id":"trivia","title":"Trivia","blocks":[{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["Chaos Rosalia, ",{"i":"Sprite-Chaos_Malachite.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"relic:chaos-malachite"}," ",{"t":"Chaos Malachite","r":"relic:chaos-malachite"},", ",{"i":"Sprite-Chaos_Lazulia.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"relic:chaos-lazulia"}," ",{"t":"Chaos Lazulia","r":"relic:chaos-lazulia"},", and ",{"i":"Sprite-Chaos_Altemanna.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"relic:chaos-altemanna"}," ",{"t":"Chaos Altemanna","r":"relic:chaos-altemanna"}," are likely references to the ",{"t":"Chaos Emeralds","x":"https://sonic.fandom.com/wiki/Chaos_Emerald"}," from the ",{"t":"Sonic the Hedgehog","x":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonic_the_Hedgehog"}," game series. They are gems that hold miraculous powers, one of the most well known being the ability to initiate super transformations."]},{"c":["The spell \"coldwaterhotwater\" and its association with Yatta Cavallo are likely references to the Ranma 1/2 manga and anime franchise, wherein several characters are cursed to transform when doused with cold water and return to normal with hot water, one such transformation being a panda."]}]}],"subs":[]}]}